chance top-1 0.0204 over 49 classes. 'ceiling' is the authored
frame through the identical path: CLIP is half-blind to 1-bit
silhouettes, so the ratio is the quotable number, not the raw score.

5 clip(s) have a zero ceiling and so no top-1 ratio: family_ad_scene_01_I, family_ad_scene_03_F, family_ad_scene_03_I, family_ad_scene_05_I, family_ad_scene_06_I.
The cause is the class design, not the solve. tests/clip_eval.py folds
I/l/1 into one class because they are the same picture, and glyph_prompt
then asks for 'the digit 1'. A serif capital I from a title card is not a
digit 1 to CLIP, so the authored frame misses too and the ratio has no
denominator. Their MRR ratios near 1.0 say shadow and target are equally
unreadable here, not that the shadow is good.

